    "body": "## Overview\n\nSkip redundant `movedim` + `reshape` tensor view operations when `dim=0` in `cuda_communicator.py`'s `reduce_scatter`.\n\n## Claims\n\n- Eliminates 2 redundant `movedim` + `contiguous` calls per `reduce_scatter(dim=0)` call\n\n## Validation\n\n- `ruff check` and `ruff format --check`: all passed\n- When `dim=0`, `movedim(0, 0)` returns the same tensor — skipping is behavior-preserving\n\n## Details\n\n`reduce_scatter` in `cuda_communicator.py` calls `movedim(0, dim)` and `.contiguous()` on both input and output. When `dim=0`, `movedim(0, 0)` is a no-op. Call `.contiguous()` directly and return the output without `movedim` when `dim=0`.\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary> Pull Request Checklist </summary>\n\n- [x] I used vLLM's `/pr-checklist` skill.\n- [x] AI assistance was used during the creation of this PR.\n\n- [x] **Design Fit:** Minimizes impact on core components, reuses existing functionality, and justifies added complexity.\n- [x] **Testing and Validation:** Validates the change and ensures any added tests are meaningful and reliable.\n- [x] **Code Quality and Style:** Keeps code and comments clear and concise.\n- [x] **Pull Request Contents:** Includes a brief summary and relevant links, supports claims with evidence, and follows the contributing guide.\n</details>\n",
